      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of a sudden, dramatic bio-evolutionary shift in a single human lifetime is not supported by current mainstream biological understanding. What you might be describing involves heightened sensory perception, which can sometimes be linked to intense states of awareness or even neurological changes. Science generally views sensory shifts as related to brain function, stress, or environmental factors rather than rapid evolution. If you're interested in the biological basis of heightened perception, exploring neuroscience might provide more concrete information.",
